  speakerName: APO LAKAY
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: '"To reach the top of the tower and see the province below, you need
    to tell someone to move upward.

    In Ilokano, ''umuli iti ngato'' means ''go
    up.''

    Use it when directing someone toward a higher place.

    Listen carefully:
    umuli iti ngato.

    Now, try saying ''umuli iti ngato'' yourself."

'
